      "sequence_position": 1,
      "problem": "Given the quartic function $f(x;a,b,c)=a{x}^{4}+b{x}^{3}+c{x}^{2},$ compute ${∇}_{b,c}\\,f.$\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" width=\"30px\" height=\"35px\" align=\"center\">${∇}_{b,c}\\,f=\\text{ }$</td>\n<td width=\"5px\" height=\"30px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"30px\" align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n\n<td width=\"5px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr> \n<td height=\"35px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>",
      "worked_solution": "To compute ${∇}_{b,c}\\,f$, we take partial derivatives with respect to $b$ and $c.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂b} & =\\frac{∂}{∂b}(a{x}^{4}+b{x}^{3}+c{x}^{2})={x}^{3} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂c} & =\\frac{∂}{∂c}(a{x}^{4}+b{x}^{3}+c{x}^{2})={x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{b,c}\\,f & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂b} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂c}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3} \\\\ {x}^{2}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
